<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian BIAT H1 profits rise 30.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Tunisian BIAT H1 profits rise 30.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisian Banque Internationale Arabe de Tunisie, the biggest private sector bank in Tunisia, said its net profits during the first half of 1997 rose 30.7 percent to 6.274 million dinars from 4.8 million dinars during the same period last year.</p>
<p>The bank's capital totals 86 million dinars owned by Tunisian private shareholders and European and Gulf banks.</p>
<p>BIAT's share was last priced 29.44 dinars at the Tunis Stock Exchange. ($=1.166 dinar)</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
